{"id":45954,"name":"Eau Claire County","slug":"eau-claire-county","state":"Wisconsin","code":"WI","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/eau-claire-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-27T12:37:31","facts":null,"bodyHtml":"<div class=\"yoast-breadcrumbs\"><span><span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/\">Home</a></span> » <span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/\">Tax Deed</a></span> » <span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/\">Tax Deed States</a></span> » <span><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/\">Wisconsin Tax Deed Investments: The Benefits of Tax Deed Sales</a></span> » <span class=\"breadcrumb_last\" aria-current=\"page\">Eau Claire County</span></span></div>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"Tg0YvmQbu8KsbDpCOxWideLPray2f4FrknIMGiwvkypUcxNm4BjjRJ1URVNMwWc3\"><iframe title=\"Beginner Tax Deed Investing (Step By Step)\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/5RJylhmyFtI?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-estimated-reading-time yoast-reading-time__wrapper\"><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__icon\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" data-icon=\"clock\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.1em\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" d=\"M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z\"></path></svg></span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__spacer\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:1em\"></span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__descriptive-text\">Estimated reading time: </span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__reading-time\">6</span><span class=\"yoast-reading-time__time-unit\"> minutes</span></p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Author:</strong>&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://taxlienschool.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">TLS Team</mark></a></strong><br><strong>Reviewed by:</strong>&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://taxlienschool.com/josh-blanchard-tax-lien-school/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Josh Blanchard</mark></a></strong><br><strong>Fact Checked by:</strong>&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://taxlienschool.com/jack-aldous-tax-lien-school/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Jack Aldous</mark></a></strong></p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p>Eau Claire County, Wisconsin, happens when the county takes ownership of a property through a court process because the owner did not pay real estate taxes. The county then auctions that property to the public. This guide explains each step and shows where you can check for current listings.</p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-table-of-contents yoast-table-of-contents\"><h3>Table of contents</h3><ul><li><a href=\"#h-what-is-a-tax-deed\" data-level=\"2\">What Is a Tax Deed?</a><ul><li><a href=\"#h-what-is-a-tax-deed-in-eau-claire-county\" data-level=\"3\">What Is a Tax Deed in Eau Claire County?</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-how-the-eau-claire-county-tax-deed-process-works\" data-level=\"3\">How the Eau Claire County Tax Deed Process Works</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-how-to-bid-on-an-eau-claire-county-tax-deed-property\" data-level=\"3\">How to Bid on an Eau Claire County Tax Deed Property</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-why-buyers-should-do-their-homework\" data-level=\"3\">Why Buyers Should Do Their Homework</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-quick-facts-table\" data-level=\"3\">Quick Facts Table</a></li><li><a href=\"#h-faq\" data-level=\"3\">FAQ</a></li></ul></li></ul></div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-what-is-a-tax-deed\"><strong>What Is a Tax Deed?</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>When a property owner does not pay real estate taxes, the debt becomes delinquent. If the taxes stay unpaid long enough, the county can take legal title to the property. This is called a tax deed. The county then sells these properties to the public to recover the unpaid taxes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-what-is-a-tax-deed-in-eau-claire-county\"><strong>What Is a Tax Deed in Eau Claire County?</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>When property taxes go unpaid long enough in Eau Claire County, the debt does not go away on its own. The county has to take legal action to collect it. In Wisconsin, that action is called an &#8220;In Rem&#8221; foreclosure. Once the court grants the foreclosure, Eau Claire County becomes the legal owner of the property. Only then does the county sell it to a new buyer through a tax deed.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Wisconsin does not sell tax lien certificates. There is no outside investor who buys the debt and waits for interest. The county itself takes the title, then resells the parcel. Since January 1, 2023, the Eau Claire County Treasurer&#8217;s Office has handled this entire process, including the tax deed and In Rem steps and the final sale.</p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-ai-summarize yoast-ai-summarize\"><h3>Key Takeaways</h3>\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list yoast-ai-summarize-list\">\n<li>Eau Claire County Tax Deed process begins with unpaid property taxes leading to an In Rem foreclosure.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The county then takes ownership and sells the property through an auction after a court judgment.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Buyers should check the county&#8217;s Tax Delinquent Property webpage and follow local auction notices for details.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>It&#8217;s crucial for buyers to conduct thorough research before bidding, as properties are sold &#8216;as is&#8217;.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For questions, contact the Eau Claire County Treasurer&#8217;s Office at 715-839-4805 or email treasurer@eauclairecounty.gov.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-how-the-eau-claire-county-tax-deed-process-works\"><strong>How the Eau Claire County Tax Deed Process Works</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The path from unpaid taxes to a public sale runs through a court case, not a simple auction sign-up. Here is how the stages usually break down.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Stage</strong></td><td><strong>What Happens</strong></td></tr><tr><td>1. Taxes go unpaid</td><td>The owner does not pay real estate taxes for a set number of years</td></tr><tr><td>2. Notice of Commencement filed</td><td>The Treasurer files this notice with the Clerk of Courts to start the In Rem foreclosure</td></tr><tr><td>3. Court hearing held</td><td>A judge reviews the case at a scheduled foreclosure hearing</td></tr><tr><td>4. County takes title</td><td>Once the court grants judgment, Eau Claire County owns the property outright</td></tr><tr><td>5. Auction list published</td><td>The county lists foreclosed parcels in the Leader-Telegram newspaper as a &#8220;Class 3&#8221; auction</td></tr><tr><td>6. Bidding period opens</td><td>The public can bid during the stated auction window</td></tr><tr><td>7. County Board approves</td><td>The County Board votes to finalize the winning bids</td></tr><tr><td>8. Deed issued</td><td>The buyer receives the deed and records it with the Register of Deeds</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>As of this writing, the county has an active In Rem case. A Notice of Commencement was filed on April 7, 2026, and the foreclosure hearing is set for September 9, 2026. This means a new batch of properties could reach auction sometime after that court date.</p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Eau-Claire-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Eau-Claire-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Eau-Claire-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Eau-Claire-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-768x512.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Eau-Claire-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1.webp\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Eau-Claire-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1.webp 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Eau-Claire-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-541x360.webp 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Eau-Claire-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-296x197.webp 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Eau-Claire-County-Wisconsin-Tax-Deed-1-768x512.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-45965 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Eau Claire County Wisconsin Tax Deed\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-how-to-bid-on-an-eau-claire-county-tax-deed-property\"><strong>How to Bid on an Eau Claire County Tax Deed Property</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-how-to wp-block-yoast-how-to-block\"><p class=\"schema-how-to-description\">Follow these steps to take part in a future sale.</p> <ol class=\"schema-how-to-steps\"><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785172242550\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\">Check the Treasurer&#8217;s &#8220;Tax Delinquent Property&#8221; webpage often.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">This page lists the current In Rem case status and links to past and upcoming auctions.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785172263219\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\">Watch for the Leader-Telegram auction notice.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">This is where the county posts the property list and the exact bidding window.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785172275440\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\">Look up the parcel using the county&#8217;s Land Records Portal.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">Review ownership history, tax bills, and assessed value before you commit to anything.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785172296054\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\">Pull deed and lien records from the Register of Deeds office.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">This helps you spot old claims tied to the land.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785172305956\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\">Confirm zoning with the local town, city, or village.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\"> A tax deed does not remove local zoning rules.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785172319598\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\">Submit your bid within the posted auction window.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\"></p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785172325671\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\">Wait for County Board approval.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\">The board must give final sign-off before any sale is complete.</p> </li><li class=\"schema-how-to-step\" id=\"how-to-step-1785172338320\"><strong class=\"schema-how-to-step-name\">Record your deed with the Register of Deeds once payment and approval are done.</strong> <p class=\"schema-how-to-step-text\"></p> </li></ol></div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-why-buyers-should-do-their-homework\"><strong>Why Buyers Should Do Their Homework</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Every property sold through this process goes &#8220;as is.&#8221; The county gives no promise about the roof, the foundation, or any debt still tied to the land. Before you bid, take these steps:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Review the parcel&#8217;s tax and ownership history through the county&#8217;s online tools.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Search Register of Deeds records for old liens or unresolved claims.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drive by the property if you can. Interior viewing is rarely offered.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Contact the local zoning office to confirm allowed use.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Set money aside for back fees, repairs, or cleanup costs.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-quick-facts-table\"><strong>Quick Facts Table</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Item</strong></td><td><strong>Detail</strong></td></tr><tr><td>County agency</td><td>Eau Claire County Treasurer (Glenda Lyons)</td></tr><tr><td>Process type</td><td>In Rem foreclosure (Wisconsin Chapter 75), then tax deed sale</td></tr><tr><td>Auction listing source</td><td>Leader-Telegram newspaper &#8220;Class 3&#8221; auction notices</td></tr><tr><td>Handling change</td><td>Treasurer took over the full process starting January 1, 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Property condition</td><td>Sold &#8220;as is,&#8221; buyer does own research</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-faq\"><strong>FAQ</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"schema-faq wp-block-yoast-faq-block\"><div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785172120587\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>What is an Eau Claire County, Wisconsin tax deed?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">It is the ownership title the county gets after winning an In Rem foreclosure case against a property with unpaid taxes. The county then sells the property to the public.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785172135633\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Does Eau Claire County sell tax liens?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">No. Like other Wisconsin counties, Eau Claire County does not sell tax lien certificates. It takes full title through the court, then sells the property itself.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785172151915\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Where can I find current auction listings?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Check the Treasurer&#8217;s Tax Delinquent Property page and watch for auction notices published in the Leader-Telegram newspaper.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785172169745\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Is there a sale happening right now?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">The county has an active In Rem case with a court hearing set for September 9, 2026. No open auction is listed at this time, so check the Treasurer&#8217;s page for updates.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785172181929\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Can I get the property back before the deed is finalized?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">The In Rem process gives owners a chance to resolve the debt before the court grants judgment. Once judgment is entered and the county takes title, that window closes.</p> </div> <div class=\"schema-faq-section\" id=\"faq-question-1785172194297\"><strong class=\"schema-faq-question\"><strong>Can I inspect a property before bidding?</strong></strong> <p class=\"schema-faq-answer\">Usually only from the outside. Properties sell &#8220;as is,&#8221; so plan to do outside research instead of an interior walkthrough.</p> </div> </div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Sources:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.eauclairecounty.gov/departments/treasurer/tax_deliquent_property\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Eau Claire Tax Delinquent Property</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.eauclairecounty.gov/departments/treasurer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Eau Claire County Treasurer</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.eauclairecounty.gov/departments/register_of_deeds/land_records\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Eau Claire Land Records</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Related Links:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-yoast-seo-related-links yoast-seo-related-links\">\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/wisconsin-property-investments-the-benefits-of-tax-deed-sales/racine-county/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Racine County</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-lien-ai-1-webinar/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Tax Lien AI-1 Webinar</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-lien/tax-lien-states/maryland-tax-liens-earn-solid-as-a-beginner/washington-county/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Washington County</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/auction-calendar-event/will-county-illinois-tax-deed-auction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Will  County IL – Tax Deed Auction</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p></p>\n<p><em>Sign up or log in to view the full content.</em></p><div id=\"popup-overlay\"></div><div id=\"signup-popup\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 20px;\"><h4>Get Instant Free Access To The Training Vault Now</h4><p>Learn how to get 18-36% returns on your investment and buy property for as little as $500 with tax lien and tax deeds.</p><div class=\"video-container\" style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 20px 0;\"><iframe src=\"https://youtube.com/embed/FkB-M8RaSHo\" allowfullscreen style=\"width: 100%; max-width: 560px; height: 315px; border: none; border-radius: 8px;\"></iframe></div><div class=\"button-container\" style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 10px;\"><button style=\"padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer;\">Sign Up for FREE Access</button><button style=\"padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; cursor: pointer;\">Already a Member? Login</button></div></div>","upcomingCount":0}